  found: ["Your first city", "The first city may stand on plains, forest, coast, mountain, or sea. A sea city is a port with a harbor, shipyard, and transport. A mountain city is strong in defense, has no port, and marches over peaks more slowly. Name the tile, queue the found-city order, then press Execute at the bottom."],
  colonize: ["Later cities", "From the second city on, scout adjacent tiles and open a conquered corridor. Colonize costs 3 person cards plus slaves and supplies. You cannot colonize the open sea (coast and land are fine). You cannot attack your own cities or guild members. Guild members share claimed tiles."],
  march: ["Marches", "A march needs an origin city and checked people. Tapping a tile only picks the target; it does not send troops. Sea travel needs a harbor and transport. War at sea also needs a trireme and a captain. Scout and reinforce at sea only need harbor and transport."],
  reports: ["Reports", "When your march arrives, a letter is written to your personal inbox. Open Reports in the header—a large board with search by victory or mission."],
  market: ["Market", "There is no market link in the game. Card trading is not part of the war screen. Fallen cards are destroyed forever."],
  guild: ["Guilds", "A guild shares claimed tiles so you can expand together. After you leave, you cannot join another guild for one month. City and guild names stay as players typed them."],
  atlas: ["Atlas", "A bird’s-eye view of the world. Search a chart name, coordinates such as 0,0, or your city, then tap a cell to enter the 3D map."],
